 "answers": {
  "Q1": {
   "answer": "The paper addresses whether the large gains neural IR models show on standard benchmarks reflect genuine generalization, given that those benchmarks evaluate models within the same distribution used for training. It targets the untested question of zero-shot retrieval generalization across new tasks and domains.",
   "locations": [
    "Abstract",
