   "confidence": 5,
   "missing": ""
  },
  "Q2": {
   "answer": "Retrieval is the first stage of high-stakes NLP pipelines (open-domain QA, fact verification, literature discovery, duplicate detection), so failures when models move to new domains matter in practice. Prior multi-dataset efforts (MultiReQA, KILT) give only partial coverage and do not measure zero-shot generalization explicitly, leaving the core question open.",
   "locations": [
    "\u00a71 \u00b61",
    "\u00a71 \u00b63-4"
